==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|copout}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[cop]]-[[out]]}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} [[avoidance|Avoidance]] or [[inadequate]] [[performance]] of a [[task]] or [[duty]]; the [[action]] of [[cop out|copping out]].
#: ''His disappearance on the day of the audition was just a '''cop-out'''.''
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} An [[excuse]] made in order to avoid performing a task or duty; a [[reason]] offered when someone cops out.
#: ''It was a '''cop-out''' to say he couldn't sign the petition because he sprained his wrist.''
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} A [[person]] who cops out.
#: ''He's always a '''cop-out''' when there's hard work to be done.''

